List of files

Simulation data processing

make_x01_file_tree.py
    make a tree of folders on x01 to store the output of compute_observable_on_trjs_x01_v3.py
compute_observable_on_trjs_x01_v3.py
    run a processing script (provided as an argument) on the data from all 12 simulations from my Arachidonic acid - AAC1/UCP1 interactions paper
    note that this is generally used by being imported into the processing script and then called there with the main processing function as its argument
x01_rotamer_solvation_secstr.py
    calculate the water hydrogen bonds, rotamer, and whether every (thr or ser) residue in every frame is on a helix that could support backbone hydrogen bonding, and return them as numpy arrays
    This provides the data for downstream methods without doing any post-processing
    outputs are in /thr_rotamers_solvation/resi_data
x01_secstr.py
    calculate the secondary structure of every threonine (or serine) at every frame (with no regard for its neighbors unlike the above)
    This is used for defining which residues are on loops
x01_nearby_waters.py
    calculate the number of waters within 3.3A of each thr (or ser) OH in each frame, by O-O distance


Analysis using the npy files generated by x01_rotamer_solvation_secstr.py

plot_rot_solv_sec_hist.ipynb
    calculate delta-delta-G (ddG) values for rotamer flipping and h-bond formation for each individual residue (aggregating data from all simulations). 
    ddG values are then averaged across residues.
    This turns out to be a bad approach because it only cares if there is a single water hydrogen bonding the residue and neglects effects
    of the broader solvation environment such as the cost of bringing the water molecule to the vicinity of the residue.
plot_rot_solv_sec_fixed_solvation.ipynb
    calculate delta-G values for rotamer flipping of each residue (aggregating data from all simulations) and the hydrogen bonding probability of each residue
    Residues are then grouped into buried, interfacial, and water exposed by hydrogen bond frequency.
    The difference between the average flipping delta-G of the buried and water exposed categories is the delta-delta-G
    --> This notebook makes the scatter and box plots
rotamer_solvation_plots.ipynb
    this also uses files from x01_secstr.py
    plot the probability of +-60 vs 180 degree rotamers for buried vs aqueous residues in the middles of TM helices (i.e. the same categories used for the analysis in plot_rot_solv_sec_fixed_solvation.ipynb)
    --> This notebook makes the bar plots
nearby_water_analysis.ipynb
    this also uses files from x01_nearby_waters.py
    make plots of the mean number of nearby waters for rotamers in the three analyzed site categories (wet and dry helices plus wet loops)


threonine_rotamer_solvation_ss.ipynb
    [currently only processes test numpy files containing a small portion of the data; lacks a loading function]
    calculate probabilities of each combination of (discrete) helicity, h-bond, and rotamer to look for correlations. Also has cells to plot observables over time. The result was that (helical) residues differ drastically in their joint h-bond-rotamer probability distributions.
plot_rot_solv_sec_transitions.ipynb
    calculate transitions between all combinations of helicity, h-bond, and rotameric states to determine whether our simulations are long enough to sample the relevant transitions enough times to obtain converged free energy estimates just by looking at the relative frequencies of simulation frames in different states. Simulations are indeed long enough (this is why error bars are calculated by averaging across residues, which differ much more than the simulation replicates). 


Draft simulation data processing; still have deprecated manually assigned residue categories

draft_analysis/threonine_hbond_calculation.ipynb
    hydrogen bond calculation with mdanalysis
draft_analysis/x01_threonine_solvation.py
    proximity-based solvation calculation with mdtraj; NOT based on threonine_hbond_calculation.ipynb
plot_rotamers.ipynb
    make bar graph of probabilities of being near different numbers of waters at sites with different (manually assigned) solvation states 

draft_analysis/threonine_rotamer_calculation.ipynb
    rotamer calculation with mdanalysis
draft_analysis/x01_threonine_rotamers.py
    rotamer calculation with mdanalysis; .py version of threonine_rotamer_calculation.ipynb
plot_rotamers.ipynb
    make bar graph of probabilities of the probabilities of different rotamers at sites with different (manually assigned) solvation states 

draft_analysis/plot_nearby_waters.ipynb
    plot test outputs of x01_nearby_waters.py


Pymol script and svg figure editing

cutaway_figure.py
    make a cutaway figure of UCP1 to illustrate the simulated system
    
rgb_protein_colors.txt

